53:20.020 --> 53:20.760
Loeb's theorem.

53:21.420 --> 53:22.400
This is another dense one.

53:22.480 --> 53:23.280
Break this down for us.

53:23.720 --> 53:25.120
What is a self-endorsing

53:25.120 --> 53:26.980
sentence in formal logic?

53:26.980 --> 53:28.900
To understand Loeb's theorem,

53:29.220 --> 53:30.020
we need to think about

53:30.020 --> 53:31.900
how formal proof systems work.

53:32.380 --> 53:32.980
A proof system

53:32.980 --> 53:34.100
is just a set of rules

53:34.100 --> 53:35.460
used to establish truth

53:35.460 --> 53:37.060
based on starting axioms.

53:37.320 --> 53:37.360
Okay.

53:38.040 --> 53:39.020
Flyxion realized

53:39.020 --> 53:40.100
that they could force

53:40.100 --> 53:41.200
the mathematical model

53:41.200 --> 53:43.160
to output a published decision

53:43.160 --> 53:44.220
by introducing

53:44.220 --> 53:45.680
a logical cheat code.

53:46.080 --> 53:46.780
If the researchers

53:46.780 --> 53:47.520
simply wrote

53:47.520 --> 53:49.200
a new mathematical axiom

53:49.200 --> 53:49.860
into the code

53:49.860 --> 53:50.360
that said

53:50.360 --> 53:51.740
whatever this formal

53:51.740 --> 53:52.700
proof system says

53:52.700 --> 53:53.400
is warranted

53:53.400 --> 53:55.180
is inherently warranted,

53:55.440 --> 53:56.420
then the system

53:56.420 --> 53:57.220
would instantly,

53:57.520 --> 53:58.720
effortlessly prove

53:58.720 --> 53:59.280
that the essay

53:59.280 --> 54:00.000
should be published.

54:00.000 --> 54:02.180
It's a circular logic cheat code.

54:03.140 --> 54:03.980
Let me try an analogy.

54:04.140 --> 54:05.280
It's like a high school student

54:05.280 --> 54:06.640
printing their own report card,

54:07.260 --> 54:08.560
